<title>CHINA: China to export thermal power equipment to Iran.</title>
<headline>China to export thermal power equipment to Iran.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>China will export nearly $200 million worth of thermal power equipment to Iran, Chinese officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The China National Machinery and Equipment Import and Export Corporation and the Shanghai Electric Company (SEC) signed a sales agreement with Iran on March 17, officials of both companies told Reuters.</p>
<p>The deal includes two 32.5 megawatt-boilers and steam turbine generator units, the officials said. They did not identify the Iranian buyer or give other financial details of the accord.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
